s in an order, the App for this feature goes in reverse    In both cases, the reason should be the verbatim text summary with the database item.    The software description should be a peer-to-peer comment, to yourself, in the future.    This makes the source file where the changes occur the bridge between internal and external.------------------------------------------    The repository tool for viewing differences between files is based on instances of commits.    A FIXIT as an information tool is a snapshot of the state of all FIXITs relative to a commit.    Each commit into the repository will include a snapshot in text form, as a managed object.    This will allow a comparison over Time to the state of FIXITs as development progresses.    A software application could use text analysis to show that all FIXITs are accounted for.------------------------------------------=====================------------------------------------------ [delete:]    In support of its educational goals, TSC LLC invents the word "FIXIT" as a placeholder for the    word chosen by the software development culture behind the ecosystem the developer works in.    The FSM of state changes to the FIXIT over Time are described by corporate project management.    The assignment of a FIXIT identifier instantiates a database entry that now will live forever.    The FIXIT database has a primary selection value for each individual and unique item.    References to values are made throughout repository metadata, without repeating the content.    Every software development organization makes up a set of conventions that must be followed.------------------------------------------ [delete:]    FIXIT keyword definition adopted for this project within this organization:        FppTnn   <format><project ID><M:missing | B:broken><integer 0-99>    The first letter defines the format of the rest of the keyword.  Every keyword in the database    that starts with 'F' wil